            <ArticleTitle>Shearing of a peripheral nerve catheter.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>760-1, table of contents</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText Label="IMPLICATIONS" NlmCategory="CONCLUSIONS">We report a previously undescribed complication of peripheral nerve catheter placement. The catheter was sheared when its stylet was removed with the placement needle still in the tissues. The lost distal fragment was identified with computed tomography scanning.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
